==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*falwaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*pel-}}.

Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|falu|lang=osx}}, Middle Dutch {{term|valu|lang=dum}}, {{term|vale|lang=dum}} (Dutch {{term|vaal|lang=nl}}), Old High German {{term|falo|lang=goh}} (German {{term|fahl|lang=de}}), Old Norse {{term|fǫlr|lang=non}}. The common Germanic is cognate with Latin {{term|pallidus|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|πελιτνός|tr=pelitnós|lang=grc}} and Old Armenian {{term|ալիք||wave, gray hair|tr=alikʿ|lang=xcl}}.

